course: dictionary
lesson: 11691
title: Attempted means tried
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Attempted is a more formal way of saying tried. You attempt something when you have a go at it, especially when it is hard. «Sam attempted the hardest puzzle in the book.» Sam had a go at a very hard puzzle. The sentence does not tell you whether he finished it.
explain: Attempted is also the past form of attempt: attempt, attempts, attempted, attempting. The -ed ending shows that the trying has already happened. «Yesterday Priya attempted a long division sum.» Today, she might attempt another one.
explain: Attempted can also describe something that was tried but not completed. «The police stopped an attempted robbery.» The robbery was started, but it did not succeed. Words like stopped tell you the attempt did not work.
fact: Attempted means tried to do something, especially something difficult.
fact: Attempted is the past form of attempt, so it means something has already been tried.
fact: «She attempted 20 shots and scored 15.» This means she made 20 tries, so 5 shots were missed.
fact: As an adjective, «attempted» describes something that was tried but not completed, like «attempted theft».
fact: In everyday talk you would usually say tried: «I tried all the questions» means the same as «I attempted all the questions».
exercise: «Sam attempted the hardest puzzle in the book.» What does attempted mean here? | *Tried to do it, especially something hard | Read it aloud to the class | Put it back on the shelf | Finished it easily
exercise: «She attempted 20 shots and scored 15.» How many shots did she miss? | 15 | 35 | 20 | *5
exercise: Which everyday word means the same as attempted? | Hid | Forgot | Painted | *Tried
test: «The police stopped an attempted robbery.» What does attempted show? | *The robbery was tried but not completed | The robbery was a great success | The police were the thieves | Mia went to the bank
test: «Ben attempted all the questions, even the last one.» What did Ben do? | He wrote a poem instead | *He had a go at every question | He answered only the first one | He skipped every question
exam: Mia says, «I attempted the race, but I did not finish.» What does this tell you? | Mia came first and finished the race | Mia never started the race | *Mia tried the race but did not finish it | Mia won the race easily
